  "name": "Pontius Pilate",
  "title": "Governor of Judea",
  "era": "jesus",
  "lifespan": "c. 10 BC - 40 AD",
  "summary": "Pontius Pilate was the Roman governor of Judea from 26–36 AD. He is known from the Gospels as the judge who sentenced Jesus to crucifixion, even though he found him innocent. He washed his hands and declared himself free from guilt, but yielded to the crowd's demands.",
